Section 80C. Deduction in respect of life insurance premia, deferred annuity, contributions to provident fund, subscription to certain equity shares or debentures, etc.—
(1) In computing the total income of an assessee, being an individual or a Hindu undivided family, there shall be deducted, in accordance with and subject to the provisions of this section, the whole of the amount paid or deposited in the previous year, being the aggregate of the sums specified in sub-section (2), as does not exceed one hundred and fifty thousand rupees.

(2) The sums referred to in sub-section (1) shall be any sums paid or deposited in the previous year by the assessee—
(i) to effect or to keep in force an insurance on the life of persons specified in sub-section (4);
(ii) to effect or to keep in force a contract for a deferred annuity, not being an annuity plan referred to in clause (j), on the life of persons specified in sub-section (4);
(iii) by way of deduction from the salary payable by or on behalf of the Government to any individual for the purpose of securing to him a deferred annuity or making provision for his spouse or children;
(iv) as a contribution to any provident fund to which the Provident Funds Act, 1925 (19 of 1925), applies;
(v) as a contribution to any recognized provident fund;
(vi) as a contribution to any approved superannuation fund;
(vii) as subscription to any such security of the Central Government or any such deposit scheme as that Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, specify in this behalf;
(viii) as subscription to any such savings certificates as defined in clause (c) of section 2 of the Government Savings Certificates Act, 1959;
(ix) as a contribution to an approved annuity plan of the Life Insurance Corporation or any other insurer;
(x) as subscription to any units of any Mutual Fund referred to in clause (23D) of section 10;
(xi) as a contribution by an individual to any pension fund set up by any Mutual Fund referred to in clause (23D) of section 10;
(xii) as subscription to any such deposit scheme of, or contribution to any such pension fund set up by, the National Housing Bank;
(xiii) as subscription to any such deposit scheme of a public sector company;
(xiv) as tuition fees (excluding any payment towards any development fees or donation or payment of similar nature), whether at the time of admission or thereafter, to any university, college, school or other educational institution situated within India, for the purpose of full-time education of any two children of such individual;
(xv) for the purposes of purchase or construction of a residential house property the income from which is chargeable to tax under the head "Income from house property";
(xvi) as subscription to equity shares or debentures forming part of any eligible issue of capital made by a public company;
(xvii) as subscription to any units of any mutual fund referred to in clause (23D) of section 10 and approved by the Board;
(xviii) as term deposit for a fixed period of not less than five years with a scheduled bank;
(xix) as subscription to any such bonds issued by the National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development;
(xx) as deposit in an account under the Senior Citizens Savings Scheme Rules, 2004;
(xxi) as five year time deposit in an account under the Post Office Time Deposit Rules, 1981;
(xxii) as a contribution by an employee of the Central Government to a specified account of the pension scheme referred to in section 80CCD.

(3) The provisions of sub-section (2) shall apply only to so much of any premium or other payment made on an insurance policy, other than a contract for a deferred annuity, as does not exceed ten per cent of the actual capital sum assured.

(4) The persons referred to in sub-section (2) shall be the individual, the spouse and any child of such individual, or any member of the Hindu undivided family.

(5) If the assessee terminates the contract of insurance or transfers house property before specified periods, the aggregate deduction allowed in previous years shall be deemed to be income of the previous year in which contract is terminated.

