Section 25. General deductions for business expenditure.—
(1) Any expenditure (not being capital expenditure or personal expenditure) laid out or expended wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the business or profession shall be deductible in computing business income.

(2) No deduction shall be allowed under sub-section (1) in respect of:
(a) expenditure incurred for any purpose which is an offence or prohibited by any law in India or outside India;
(b) expenditure incurred to provide any benefit or perquisite to a person where acceptance of such benefit is in violation of any law or conduct regulations;
(c) expenditure incurred on activities relating to corporate social responsibility under section 135 of the Companies Act, 2013.

