Section 10. Incomes not included in total income.—
In computing the total income of a previous year of any person, any income falling within any of the following clauses shall not be included—
(1) agricultural income;
(2) any sum received by an individual as a member of a Hindu undivided family, where such sum has been paid out of the family income or estate;
(2A) in the case of a person being a partner of a firm, any share in the total income of the firm;
(10) any death-cum-retirement gratuity received under the revised Pension Rules of the Central Government;
(10AA) any payment received by an employee as cash equivalent of leave salary in respect of earned leave at the credit of his account at the time of retirement;
(10D) any sum received under a life insurance policy, including bonus on such policy, subject to statutory limits;
(23C) any income received by any person on behalf of approved educational institutions, medical institutions, or charitable trusts;
(23D) any income of a Mutual Fund registered under the SEBI Act, 1992.

