Section 2. Definitions.—
In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,—
(1) "agricultural income" means rent, revenue, or income derived from land situated in India and used for agricultural operations;
(2) "assessee" means any person liable to pay tax or in respect of whom any proceeding under this Act is initiated;
(3) "tax year" means the financial year beginning on the 1st day of April;
(4) "capital asset" means property of any description held by an assessee, excluding trading stock, personal effects, and rural agricultural land;
(5) "income" includes all receipts, profits, gains, dividends, perquisites, and statutory accretions chargeable under this Act;
(6) "person" includes an individual, HUF, company, firm, LLP, association of persons, local authority, or artificial juridical person.
